  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34675904",
      "title": "Submitting Forms Programmatically",
      "lectureOrder": 66,
      "videoOrder": 60,
      "sourceHash": "732b35bbd1ba480563497babe4665ef899d947d374f875778c259906b23da02d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.74,
          "en": "Now we continued our work on this action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.74,
          "end": 6.6,
          "en": "Before we now switch to some loaders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.6,
          "end": 8.79,
          "en": "There are two additional things I want to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.79,
          "end": 9.697,
          "en": "with this form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.697,
          "end": 12.84,
          "en": "I want to switch from the built in form component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.84,
          "end": 14.91,
          "en": "to Remix form component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.91,
          "end": 17.37,
          "en": "But before we do that, and before I repeat",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.37,
          "end": 18.904,
          "en": "why we might want to do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 18.904,
          "end": 21.12,
          "en": "I want to do something else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 21.12,
          "end": 23.88,
          "en": "I want to show you how you could also submit a form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 23.88,
          "end": 27.36,
          "en": "programmatically if you needed to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.36,
          "end": 29.55,
          "en": "Now it's very important to understand that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.55,
          "end": 33.51,
          "en": "in many cases you would not want to programmatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.51,
          "end": 36.87,
          "en": "submit a form because the default behavior of the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.87,
          "end": 39.63,
          "en": "which generates an HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.63,
          "end": 42.78,
          "en": "with the method you specify here and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.78,
          "end": 47.7,
          "en": "with the data included already is quite nice to have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.7,
          "end": 49.23,
          "en": "But, there are situations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.23,
          "end": 50.22,
          "en": "where you do want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 50.22,
          "end": 52.74,
          "en": "submit a form programmatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 52.74,
          "end": 53.573,
          "en": "for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 53.573,
          "end": 56.614,
          "en": "because it should be submitted when some timer times out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 56.614,
          "end": 59.25,
          "en": "to automatically log a user out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 59.25,
          "end": 60.9,
          "en": "after a certain time spent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 60.9,
          "end": 64.048,
          "en": "Or because for whatever reason you want to run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 64.048,
          "end": 67.53,
          "en": "some additional client site of validation logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 67.53,
          "end": 70.44,
          "en": "besides using these browser built in attributes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 70.44,
          "end": 72.123,
          "en": "which are recommended though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 73.17,
          "end": 74.34,
          "en": "But, if you would want to do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 74.34,
          "end": 75.75,
          "en": "you could add a new function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 75.75,
          "end": 79.2,
          "en": "'submitHandler' for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 79.2,
          "end": 82.59,
          "en": "and add the 'onSubmit' attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 82.59,
          "end": 83.47,
          "en": "to your form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 84.45,
          "end": 87.176,
          "en": "and point at 'submitHandler'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 87.176,
          "end": 89.52,
          "en": "there you then get the event object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 89.52,
          "end": 92.49000000000001,
          "en": "and you could call 'event.preventDefault' to prevent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 92.49000000000001,
          "end": 95.22,
          "en": "that browser default of generating that event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 95.22,
          "end": 98.61,
          "en": "which again is what you typically want to have though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 98.61,
          "end": 101.49000000000001,
          "en": "So typically you don't wanna prevent it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 101.49000000000001,
          "end": 104.94,
          "en": "However, before Remix, in most other React apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 104.94,
          "end": 108.03,
          "en": "you probably always did that because there you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 108.03,
          "end": 111.66,
          "en": "did have to manually send some HTTP request to your back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 111.66,
          "end": 114.24000000000001,
          "en": "And then, but with Remix, the idea is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 114.24000000000001,
          "end": 116.85,
          "en": "that you embrace these browser standards and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 116.85,
          "end": 119.943,
          "en": "that Remix connects back and front and for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 120.78,
          "end": 122.97,
          "en": "But if for whatever reason you would want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 122.97,
          "end": 126.84,
          "en": "add an extra client site validation step driven",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 126.84,
          "end": 130.08,
          "en": "by your own Javascript code, then you would need to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 130.08,
          "end": 133.575,
          "en": "prevent that default so that you then can perform",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 133.575,
          "end": 136.59,
          "en": "your own validation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 136.59,
          "end": 139.82999999999998,
          "en": "Here, we could then get some data entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 139.82999999999998,
          "end": 140.91,
          "en": "into one of the inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 140.91,
          "end": 143.25,
          "en": "and check whether it's valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 143.25,
          "end": 145.82999999999998,
          "en": "And once we perform that validation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 145.82999999999998,
          "end": 147.51,
          "en": "and I'm not going to add the code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 147.51,
          "end": 149.401,
          "en": "because it really doesn't add anything to this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 149.401,
          "end": 152.22,
          "en": "but imagine that here we're checking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 152.22,
          "end": 156.09,
          "en": "whether title, amount and so on are valid on the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 156.09,
          "end": 157.98,
          "en": "and after we perform to that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 157.98,
          "end": 159.36,
          "en": "we still might want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 159.36,
          "end": 160.299,
          "en": "submit the data to our back and of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 160.299,
          "end": 164.575,
          "en": "so we still want to that we just wanted to squeeze",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 164.575,
          "end": 166.893,
          "en": "in that extra step on the front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 167.88,
          "end": 170.94,
          "en": "So now we wanna submit to the forum programmatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 170.94,
          "end": 173.67000000000002,
          "en": "because we now need to trigger the submission on our own",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 173.67000000000002,
          "end": 176.82,
          "en": "in our own code because we prevented that default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 176.82,
          "end": 178.77,
          "en": "which we did have to do so that we could",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 178.77,
          "end": 182.13,
          "en": "squeeze in our own validation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 182.13,
          "end": 185.04,
          "en": "If you then want to submit the form programmatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 185.04,
          "end": 188.1,
          "en": "you can do this with help of the use submit hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 188.1,
          "end": 192.162,
          "en": "which is imported from at Remix run slash React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 192.162,
          "end": 196.89,
          "en": "Use.Submit gives you access to a submit function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 196.89,
          "end": 200.19,
          "en": "which you can call to basically do the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 200.19,
          "end": 201.96,
          "en": "That happens when a button is clicked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 201.96,
          "end": 206.96,
          "en": "in a form to send an HTPP request to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 207.15,
          "end": 209.49,
          "en": "Now submit takes two arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 209.49,
          "end": 213.36,
          "en": "The first argument is simply the data you wanna submit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 213.36,
          "end": 216.12,
          "en": "and you can simply point at event target here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 216.12,
          "end": 219.6,
          "en": "so at the form which was submitted here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 219.6,
          "end": 221.1,
          "en": "and Remix will then automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 221.1,
          "end": 222.96,
          "en": "extract the data from that form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 222.96,
          "end": 224.31,
          "en": "So that's quite convenient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 225.48,
          "end": 228.704,
          "en": "The second argument is then an object describing where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 228.704,
          "end": 231.96,
          "en": "and how that request should be sent to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 231.96,
          "end": 234.36,
          "en": "And here you can, for example, set your action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 234.36,
          "end": 237.39,
          "en": "So the path to which it should be sent like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 237.39,
          "end": 239.97,
          "en": "though you can omit that if it's the same path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 239.97,
          "end": 241.84,
          "en": "as the route you are currently on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 242.7,
          "end": 245.32,
          "en": "and you can set the method to post, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 246.21,
          "end": 249.9,
          "en": "and that then will submit the form programmatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 249.9,
          "end": 253.23,
          "en": "Again, in the end it does the same thing this thing does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 253.23,
          "end": 256.11,
          "en": "but it allows you to execute some extra code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 256.11,
          "end": 260.553,
          "en": "before the HTTP request is created and sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 261.63,
          "end": 263.31,
          "en": "With that, however, you will notice that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 263.31,
          "end": 264.91,
          "en": "if we now save everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 266.19,
          "end": 267.78,
          "en": "and we go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 267.78,
          "end": 272.78,
          "en": "and I add a second expense for 119.99, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 274.08,
          "end": 275.211,
          "en": "if I click save expense, we got the same behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 275.211,
          "end": 276.044,
          "en": "as before this request was sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 276.044,
          "end": 281.044,
          "en": "and it ends up in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 282.45,
          "end": 285.48,
          "en": "It's now just a bit more complicated than before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 285.48,
          "end": 288.27,
          "en": "but you might have good reasons for doing it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 288.27,
          "end": 291.75,
          "en": "because you maybe wanted to squeeze in some extra code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 291.75,
          "end": 293.7,
          "en": "Here, I'm going to comment it out though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 293.7,
          "end": 296.4,
          "en": "because I don't need it, I'm also going to comment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 296.4,
          "end": 298.71,
          "en": "out the on submit handler, therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 298.71,
          "end": 301.62,
          "en": "but I wanted to show you that this hook exists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 301.62,
          "end": 304.32,
          "en": "Also going to comment out this and remove this import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 304.32,
          "end": 307.113,
          "en": "because there are situations where you might need it.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
